<h1>k-ary Huffman coding</h1>
<p>
(algorithm)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
A minimal variable-length coding based on the frequency of each character.  Similar to a <a href="huffmanCoding.html"><em>Huffman coding</em></a>, but joins k trees into a <a href="karyTree.html"><em>k-ary tree</em></a> at each step, and uses k symbols for each level.
</p>


<p>
<em>Note:
The coding at each stage has k symbols, not just 2 (0 or 1) like traditional Huffman.  If k is a power of two, that is, k=2<sup>n</sup>, every symbol can be represented by n bits.</em>
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>
